# Advanced Static Analysis 
[Practice Analysis](https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/pti/latest/analytics/watson/analyze_text.html)

Now that you've got text analytics working, let's dig into more advanced static analysis.

## Objective
You will learn how to use Watson NLU services, which provides advanced capabilities for sentiment analysis, named entity extraction, keyword extraction, and much more from a piece of text. You'll also learn how to integrate it with IBM's Node.js SDK for Watson.

## Prerequisites
* Familiarity with IBM Cloud and NLU services
* Node.js installed on your local machine
* Some text to analyze

## Steps
### Step 1--------------------            Assume.That(New_Ret || New_arrListCount != Old_arrListCount);
        }

        [PexMethod]
        [PexEntryPoint]
        public void PUT_Contains_Test(ArrayList arrList, int x)
        {
            PUT_ContainsContract(arrList, x);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$count", arrList.Count);
        }
    }
}
```

